WEBVTT

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:03.668
Apple’s first folding iPhone

00:00:03.668 --> 00:00:05.895
starts at $1,999.

00:00:05.895 --> 00:00:07.729
But the fold itself works out

00:00:07.729 --> 00:00:09.215
to about 73 cents a day.

00:00:09.215 --> 00:00:10.670
Here’s the math.

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:13.830
Closed, it’s a 5.4-inch phone,

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.660
about the size of a passport.

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:18.371
Open, it’s a 7.6-inch screen.

00:00:18.861 --> 00:00:21.041
Folding screens usually
show a crease,

00:00:21.041 --> 00:00:22.900
and reflections give it away.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.630
Apple’s fix is a matte
nano-texture finish.

00:00:25.630 --> 00:00:29.155
It scatters reflections,
so the crease shows less.

00:00:29.945 --> 00:00:32.318
You can pay it all up front,

00:00:32.318 --> 00:00:34.243
or $83.29 a month.

00:00:34.243 --> 00:00:37.143
But 24 payments still
add up to the full price.

00:00:37.143 --> 00:00:40.033
Monthly is a schedule,
not a discount.

00:00:40.823 --> 00:00:42.863
So divide by days instead.

00:00:42.863 --> 00:00:46.433
Keep it two years: $2.74 a day.

00:00:46.433 --> 00:00:48.703
Three years: $1.83.

00:00:48.703 --> 00:00:50.413
Four: $1.37.

00:00:51.203 --> 00:00:54.023
The iPhone 18 Pro,
with the same storage,

00:00:54.023 --> 00:00:56.230
costs $800 less.

00:00:56.620 --> 00:00:58.380
So the real question is this:

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:01.244
is the fold worth $800 to you?

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:05.066
Over three years,
that’s 73 cents a day.

00:01:05.156 --> 00:01:06.836
Unfold it ten times a day,

00:01:06.836 --> 00:01:10.286
and each opening
costs about 7 cents.

00:01:10.286 --> 00:01:11.586
Once a day, 73.

00:01:12.476 --> 00:01:14.086
Two numbers are still missing.

00:01:14.086 --> 00:01:16.376
One: what it will be worth
when you sell it.

00:01:16.376 --> 00:01:17.926
Nobody knows yet.

00:01:17.926 --> 00:01:21.436
Two: what the folding screen
costs to fix without AppleCare.

00:01:21.436 --> 00:01:23.477
Apple hasn’t published that.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:26.967
So before pre-orders open
on October 16,

00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:28.667
ask three things.

00:01:28.667 --> 00:01:30.854
Will I use the big screen
every day?

00:01:30.854 --> 00:01:32.824
Will I keep it
three years or more?

00:01:32.824 --> 00:01:34.654
Would I still buy it
at full price,

00:01:34.654 --> 00:01:36.403
not split into payments?

00:01:37.293 --> 00:01:38.403
Don’t price the phone.

00:01:38.403 --> 00:01:39.746
Price the fold.
